lines=['## Latest follow-up — constant-width boards (Mode B default)','','The latest Producer direction wins: **Mode B is the default**, superseding the shrinking 5×5 choice in the original section 4 below. This deliberately makes 5×5 cells larger again; Mode A remains available for the earlier smaller-cell preference. No gameplay/progress, art or mockups changed.','','### One product switch','','`GAME_CONFIG.boardSizingMode` in **config.js** is the only switch: `\'B\'` = constant-width; `\'A\'` = target 52px cells/growing board. There is no UI, query-string or saved-progress override. All active and solved boards share the same sizing helpers in layout.js. Screenshots of A use an isolated test-only module substitution, not another shipped setting. A future A/B change is a runtime edit and needs a cache rebuild/test.','','### Reference measurement','','The supplied Meowdoku raster is **1080×2340**. Its solid white outer frame spans **x=15…1064 inclusive = 1050px** at six straight-edge interior rows. Board/screen = **1050/1080 = 35/36 = 97.2222%** (JPEG edge uncertainty about ±1px per side). The colored-tile span at row 800 is 1016px (94.07%); outer frame is the consistent board metric used here. Physical screenshot pixels are not CSS pixels. Evidence: `reference-sizing-measurement.json`, `reference-sizing-annotated.png`.','','Mode B uses **35/36 of the app width** for every grid, constrained only by the existing 440px app maximum. At the requested widths this leaves approximately **5.72px margins at 412** / **5px at 360**, matching the reference proportions. Frame/gap/padding remain unchanged.','','### Measured A → B table (CSS px)','','Cell values are the **minimum actual button width** across the grid; grid subpixel rounding can differ by ~0.02px. All button heights also meet 44px.','','|Viewport|Grid / level|A board|A cell min|B board (default)|B cell min|','|--|--|--:|--:|--:|--:|']
for w,h in [(412,915),(360,780)]:
 for n in[5,6,7]:
  a=next(x for x in rows if x['mode']=='A'and x['viewport']==f'{w}x{h}'and x['n']==n);b=next(x for x in rows if x['mode']=='B'and x['viewport']==f'{w}x{h}'and x['n']==n)
  lines.append(f"|{w}×{h}|{n}×{n} / {b['level']}|{a['board_px']:.2f}|{a['minimum_cell_px']:.2f}|**{b['board_px']:.2f}**|**{b['minimum_cell_px']:.2f}**|")
lines+=['','The narrowest B target is **44.28px** on 360px 7×7; 412px 7×7 is **51.50px**, above 48px. No board clips horizontally. Solved controls remain a separate no-scroll viewport layout; normal, boss 10, boss 30 and Daily are re-tested at both requested sizes (eight cases).','','### Captures, tests and local cache','','Six exact **412×915 PNGs**, level 3 / level 9 (6×6) / level 21 (7×7) in both modes: `screenshots-v3.1/sizing/{A,B}-level-{3,9,21}-{5x5,6x6,7x7}.png`. Side-by-side sheet including the original reference: **sizing-A-vs-B.png**. Raw per-mode DOM measurements: `sizing-{A,B}-{412,360}-followup.json`; aggregate: `sizing-A-vs-B.json`. All six captures and the comparison sheet were visually checked for clipping, overlap and readability.','','Full current test counts and offline checks are in section 7 / `TEST-SUMMARY-v3.1.json`. New A/B coverage includes all twelve viewport/grid combinations, minimum targets, reference-width uniformity and zero browser errors. The original section 4 and `sizing-before-after-v3.1.json` remain **historical Mode A** evidence, not the current default.','','Before this follow-up, snapshotted 45 local runtime/doc files under `sizing-followup-before/`, hashes in `sizing-followup-before-sha256.json`; previous report retained as `ROUND-v3.1-before-sizing.md`. Shipped backups and the frozen v3 runtime tar remain untouched.','','Prepared newer local cache: **'+cache+'**, replacing the earlier local `capydoku-v3.1-63e8bdeebfd7`. **Not pushed or published.** No new archive was requested/generated. Real iPhone/S24 and physical haptics remain unverified.']
(D/'SIZING-FOLLOWUP-v3.1.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
fontpath='/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans.ttf';font=ImageFont.truetype(fontpath,17);title=ImageFont.truetype(fontpath,24);small=ImageFont.truetype(fontpath,15)
